From 42137732cb33acd4a86afdd5a43d5b7f25a3e173 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:38:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/45] decide: protect wanted cache entries from trimming;
 restore fault mode

fill_slot snapshotted the evicted slot before it looked up the wanted
entry, so a full cache could drop exactly that entry (A,B,C,A at
--decide-prefix-cache 2 rebuilt A). run_request now collects the
hashes of every slot it fills; the trim after a snapshot drops the
least recently used entry that is not wanted, and drops the new
snapshot itself when only wanted entries are left (cache_victim).
info protects the slot 0 prefix it fills. test-decide-cache checks the
choice without a model.

LLAMA_DECIDE_FAULT=restore passes the first cache restore after start a
snapshot one byte short, so llama_state_seq_set_data fails after the
first part of a hybrid or iSWA state is in; the slot is cleared, the
entry dropped and the prefix decoded (spec 6.2). The one-shot flag is
now consumed only by its own mode: the round loop cleared it for every
mode, so "restore" never fired. llama-decide --help lists the mode.
